{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Elder Affairs to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate document relative to establish transparency and accountability for assisted living residences.\r\n\r\n","BillNumber":"S2721","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J44","Name":"Joint Committee on Elder Affairs","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J44","ResponseDate":"2024-04-05T13:33:56.763"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2721/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, April 16, 2024 -- The committee on  Elder Affairs , to whom was referred the petition (accompanied by resolve, Senate, No. 388) of Mark C. Montigny, Kay Khan, Paul A. Schmid, III and Christopher Hendricks that provisions be made for an investigation and study by a special commission (including members of the General Court) to establish transparency and accountability for assisted living residences, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2721).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Elder Affairs be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate document numbered 388 relative to establish transparency and accountability for assisted living residences.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J44","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J44"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}